// OpenPaw body-language and needs trainer: lesson + practice content as data.
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
//
// Rules for contributors (see CONTRIBUTING.md, "Safety boundary"):
// - every lesson and practice card carries `sources: [url, ...]`;
// - describe what a signal *often* or *can* mean, never a dog's emotion as fact;
// - no diagnosis, no treatment, no training protocol beyond widely accepted force-free basics;
// - anything the research disagrees about is marked in `contested`.
//
// `art` objects are drawn by drawDog() in learn.js (one side-view line dog, facing right):
//   view: 'body' | 'head'        posture: loose | stiff | crouch | turn | paw | lie | sniff | chew | bow
//   ears: neutral | forward | back | flat     eye: soft | whale | hard | closed
//   mouth: loose | closed | tense | lick | yawn | snarl     tail: mid | high | low | tucked
//   wag: none | loose | fast        hackles: bool        prop: hand | dog | person | chew | bowl | null
//   marks: [[featureName, label], ...] become numbered gold markers + a legend.

